Rule 2 (filter should be a 4-D tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 4 (filter and out_backprop should have the same data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (strides should be a list of ints and its length is equal to the number of dimensions of input_sizes.)
{v_1 : list(int), v_2 : tensor} |= v_1.len = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 7 (data_format should be either "NHWC" or "NCHW")
{v_1 : str} |= (v_1 = "NHWC") ∨ (v_1 = "NCHW")
>>
Rule 8 (dilations should be a list of ints and its length should be 4)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= v_1.len = 4
>>
Rule 9 (dilations in the batch and depth dimensions must be 1)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= v_1[0] = 1 ∧ v_1[3] = 1
>>
Rule 11 (input_sizes should have at least 4 elements)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 4
>>
Rule 13 (Check if input_sizes has positive elements)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 19 (padding should be either "SAME" or "VALID" or a list of lists of ints.)
{v_1 : str ⊎ list(list(int))} |= (v_1 = "SAME") ∨ (v_1 = "VALID")
>>
Rule 27 (The number of strides must be equal to the rank of input if input is given by input_sizes.)
{v_1 : list(int), v_2 : tensor} |= v_1.len = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 33 (padding should be either "SAME" or "VALID")
{v_1 : str} |= (v_1 = "SAME") ∨ (v_1 = "VALID")
>>
Rule 41 (Shape of filter must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 54 (If padding is explicit, the padding list's dimension should match the input dimension.)
{v_1 : list(list(int)), v_2 : tensor} |= v_1.len = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 66 (The first dimension of input_sizes and out_backprop must be equal if data_format is NHWC)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_3 = "NHWC" then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 67 (The second dimension of input_sizes and out_backprop must be equal if data_format is NCHW)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_3 = "NCHW" then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 79 (The height and width dimensions of the filter must be positive.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 80 (In channels of filter must be equal to the channels of the input when data format is NHWC)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_3 = "NHWC" then shape(v_1, 2) = shape(v_2, 3)
>>
Rule 88 (The last dimension of filter should be positive.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 91 (If data format is NCHW, then the channel dimension of input and output should match.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_3 = "NCHW" then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 101 (If data format is NHWC, the channel dimension of the filter should match the last dimension of input_sizes.)
